    "summary": "Migrated the fleet telemetry library from API v1 to v2. Pose now carries the unit quaternion as primary orientation with roll/pitch/yaw kept as derived back-compat fields (millidegree-quantised, so existing exact assertions like yaw == 87.0 still hold); all rotation math uses sign-invariant quaternion formulas with defensive normalisation. The client parses qx/qy/qz/qw, validates the 6x6 covariance, derives scalar noise as sqrt(trace(P_pos)/3) (bit-exact with v1 for isotropic fixtures, preserving fusion weights), and requires health; endpoints moved to /v2 with api_version v2. Added the health alert (MIN_HEALTH = 0.5, overridable like other thresholds). Fixtures swapped to the exact openapi_v2 fleet example as fleet_v2.json with fleet_v1.json removed; test edits limited to endpoint literals, health-alert additions, and three new tests (health alert, threshold/override, quaternion sign invariance).",
